Vox (Scouter SSH) — a mosh terminal for the Even Realities G1 under the ScouterKit firmware.
Copyright the ScouterKit authors. GPL-3.0-or-later (LICENSE), because it includes mosh.

It includes:
- mosh 1.4.0 (https://mosh.org): GPL-3.0-or-later with the OpenSSL linking exception (LICENSE).
- OpenSSL 3.5.9 (libcrypto, https://openssl-library.org): Apache-2.0 (licenses/openssl.txt).
- Protocol Buffers 21.12 (lite runtime, https://protobuf.dev): BSD-3-Clause (licenses/protobuf.txt).
- JSch, the mwiede fork (https://github.com/mwiede/jsch): BSD-3-Clause (licenses/jsch.txt).
- Bouncy Castle (https://www.bouncycastle.org): MIT (licenses/bouncycastle.txt).
- Departure Mono Nerd Font Mono (Nerd Fonts v3.5.1): SIL Open Font License 1.1, its icons under their own
  licences (licenses/departure_mono_nerd.txt, scouter_kit/third_party/departure_mono_nerd).
- sherpa-onnx 1.13.8 (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx; its Android JNI library and part of its Kotlin API,
  scouter_kit/third_party/sherpa_onnx_kotlin): Apache-2.0 (licenses/sherpa-onnx.txt), with ONNX Runtime
  (https://onnxruntime.ai) linked into it: MIT (licenses/onnxruntime.txt). Voice commands only. The speech
  models are not in the app: it downloads NVIDIA's Parakeet TDT 0.6B v2 (CC-BY-4.0, as converted for
  sherpa-onnx) and Silero VAD (MIT) when asked, checked by SHA-256.
- liblc3 1.1.3 (https://github.com/google/liblc3): Apache-2.0 (licenses/liblc3.txt, scouter_kit/third_party/liblc3),
  for the glasses' microphone.
- ScouterKit's C++ library (scouter_kit/src): MIT (scouter_kit/LICENSE), with
  - moodycamel ConcurrentQueue 1.0.5 (https://github.com/cameron314/concurrentqueue): Simplified BSD
    (licenses/concurrentqueue.txt, scouter_kit/third_party/concurrentqueue);
  - TinyCrypt 0.2.8's SHA-256 (https://github.com/intel/tinycrypt): BSD-3-Clause (licenses/tinycrypt.txt,
    scouter_kit/third_party/tinycrypt).

The source tree also has the Gradle 8.10.2 wrapper (gradlew, gradlew.bat, gradle/wrapper/; https://gradle.org):
Apache-2.0, as gradlew's header says. It is a build tool, not part of the app.
